        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "TOUCHSTONE.\n“So-so” is good, very good, very excellent good. And yet it is not, it is but so-so. Art thou wise?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@142987/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 11,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@142987/line-2",
          "start": 12,
          "end": 111,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 673362,
        "end": 673504,
        "line": 25271,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap04/p@142987",
        "anchor": "sceneV_4.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "TOUCHSTONE.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 11
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143133",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "WILLIAM.\nAy, sir, I have a pretty wit.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143133/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143133/line-2",
          "start": 9,
          "end": 38,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 673508,
        "end": 673576,
        "line": 25277,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap04/p@143133",
        "anchor": "sceneV_4.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "WILLIAM.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143205",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "TOUCHSTONE.\nWhy, thou sayst well. I do now remember a saying: “The fool doth think he is wise, but the wise man knows himself to be a fool.” The heathen philosopher, when he had a desire to eat a grape, would open his lips when he put it into his mouth, meaning thereby that grapes were made to eat and lips to open. You do love this maid?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143205/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 11,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143205/line-2",
          "start": 12,
          "end": 339,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 673580,
        "end": 673953,
        "line": 25282,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap04/p@143205",
        "anchor": "sceneV_4.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "TOUCHSTONE.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 11
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143582",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "WILLIAM.\nI do, sir.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143582/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143582/line-2",
          "start": 9,
          "end": 19,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 673957,
        "end": 674006,
        "line": 25291,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap04/p@143582",
        "anchor": "sceneV_4.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "WILLIAM.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143635",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "TOUCHSTONE.\nGive me your hand. Art thou learned?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143635/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 11,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143635/line-2",
          "start": 12,
          "end": 48,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 674010,
        "end": 674088,
        "line": 25296,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap04/p@143635",
        "anchor": "sceneV_4.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "TOUCHSTONE.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 11
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143717",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "WILLIAM.\nNo, sir.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143717/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143717/line-2",
          "start": 9,
          "end": 17,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 674092,
        "end": 674139,
        "line": 25301,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap04/p@143717",
        "anchor": "sceneV_4.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "WILLIAM.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143768",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "TOUCHSTONE.\nThen learn this of me: to have is to have. For it is a figure in rhetoric that drink, being poured out of cup into a glass, by filling the one doth empty the other. For all your writers do consent that ipse is “he.” Now, you are not ipse, for I am he.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [
        {
          "tag": "i",
          "start": 214,
          "end": 218
        },
        {
          "tag": "i",
          "start": 245,
          "end": 249
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143768/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 11,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@143768/line-2",
          "start": 12,
          "end": 263,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 674143,
        "end": 674453,
        "line": 25306,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap04/p@143768",
        "anchor": "sceneV_4.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "TOUCHSTONE.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 11
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@144082",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "WILLIAM.\nWhich he, sir?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@144082/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@144082/line-2",
          "start": 9,
          "end": 23,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 674457,
        "end": 674510,
        "line": 25314,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap04/p@144082",
        "anchor": "sceneV_4.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "WILLIAM.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@144139",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "TOUCHSTONE.\nHe, sir, that must marry this woman. Therefore, you clown, abandon—which is in the vulgar, “leave”—the society—which in the boorish is “company”—of this female—which in the common is “woman”; which together is, abandon the society of this female, or, clown, thou perishest; or, to thy better understanding, diest; or, to wit, I kill thee, make thee away, translate thy life into death, thy liberty into bondage. I will deal in poison with thee, or in bastinado, or in steel. I will bandy with thee in faction; will o’errun thee with policy. I will kill thee a hundred and fifty ways! Therefore tremble and depart.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@144139/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 11,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "as-you-like-it/sceneV_4.1/p@144139/line-2",
          "start": 12,
          "end": 625,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 674514,
        "end": 675176,
        "line": 25319,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap04/p@144139",
        "anchor": "sceneV_4.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "TOUCHSTONE.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 11
      }
    },
